    "result_text": "Done. I agreed with the finding and restructured accordingly.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Reverted `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** to its original single-purpose form \u2014 it only maps the entity to the DTO and sends the 201.\n- **Added `AuditOwnerCreated`**, a dedicated step holding the documented static `AUDIT` logger and emitting the one audit line (id, customerCode, registrationDate) from `@Val Owner`.\n- **Wired it into `owners.POST.yml`** between `save` and `respond` (`save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond`), under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding write steps. Placing it after `save` keeps the owner id populated; placing it before `respond` keeps responding free of the side effect.\n\nThis matches the codebase's one-step-one-responsibility idiom and the `Audit<E>Created` style of composing small steps with `next:`, and the audit step is now independently reorderable/testable.\n\nThe audit line still emits as expected (`AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-05`) and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
