    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe audit logging is bolted into the responder step, which breaks the one-step-one-responsibility idiom this codebase is built on.\n\n- `RespondWithOwnerCreated` is, per the naming conventions in AGENTS.md, a `RespondWith<E>Created` step whose job is to map the entity to a DTO and send the 201. It now does two unrelated things: respond *and* emit an audit record. The audit emission is a distinct side effect, not part of responding.\n- The idiomatic structure here is a separate step in the pipeline \u2014 e.g. an `AuditOwnerCreated` function class wired with `next:` ahead of the responder (reading the owner via `@Val Owner`). That keeps each class single-purpose, makes the audit step independently testable/reorderable, and matches how the rest of the endpoints compose small steps rather than accreting behavior into one class.\n- As written, the responder is on its way to becoming a catch-all: the next cross-cutting concern (metrics, events) would likely get dropped in here too, since there's now precedent. Pulling audit into its own step avoids that drift.\n\nThe logger definition itself (dedicated `AUDIT` channel, static final, documented) is fine \u2014 it's the *placement* of the emission that should move to its own pipeline step.",
